From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wooseong Kim <innocarpe@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] fix(vendor): satisfy strict clippy baseline

Use portable dunce canonicalization in pager tests and test helpers,
rewrite boolean comparisons as boolean assertions, collapse an identical
feature-gated expected value, make the fast-worktree GC sleeper a guarded
test fixture so it is killed and waited even if the test panics, and run
auth retry budget turn tests on a large-stack current-thread runtime. Align
gcloud-storage's JWT feature with the shell's rust_crypto jsonwebtoken backend
so provider selection cannot race into the aws-lc-rs default-provider
placeholder in vendored auth tests. Allow memory-trace sample rotation tests to
tolerate unrelated valid process-global trace events while retaining sample
coverage. Make the remaining full-workspace tests deterministic under parallel
CI: use a wider real-time auth lock budget with bounded slack, separate raw
restore caps from a non-vacuous symlink check, preserve client kinds while
process chat mode is hard-disabled, synchronize the single-flight test at its
first atomic claim, and capture the terminal grandchild PID through a bounded
file handshake.

